{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/m28eqd","slideIndex":4,"text":"AABB endpoint union contains any linearly interpolated vertex. A linear simplex lies in the convex hull of its vertices. Axis-wise inflation by δ/2 on both primitives conservatively admits Euclidean separation ≤δ. ⊕ denotes Minkowski addition. Instantaneous samples use t0=t1; interval record encloses the full path."}
